    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations to a student’s level. They can generate step-by-step solutions, clarify misconceptions, and offer interactive practice. In classrooms, they can act as tutors or provide instant feedback. This makes math more accessible, especially for students who struggle with traditional teaching methods."
